{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$e^x\\cos(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $e^x$ and $\\cos(x)$.\n\nTherefore, the derivative of the expression can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(e^x\\cos(x)\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(e^x\\right)\\cos(x)+e^x\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\cos(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=e^x\\cdot\\cos(x)+e^x\\cdot (-\\sin(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }e^x\\text{ and }\\cos(x)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=e^x(\\cos(x)-\\sin(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(e^x\\cos(x)\\right)=e^x(\\cos(x)-\\sin(x))$\n\nor any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(e^x\\cos(x)\\right)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"e^{x}\\left(\\cos\\left(x\\right)-\\sin\\left(x\\right)\\right)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
